<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rasamanjari</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rasamanjari of Bhanudatta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rasamanjari ('bouquet of delight') is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poem by Bhanudatta that classifies types of lovers, heroes and heroines. It became a favourite subject of Indian court painting, and the illustrated series made at Basohli in the late 17th century, including a set signed by the painter Devidasa in 1694–1695, are among the masterpieces of Pahari painting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rasamanjari.jpg" alt="Rasamanjari" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin spaink · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanjore-style_Carnatic_tambura.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
